12. COMMIT MESSAGE RULE
===============================================================================

Every repository that receives changes must receive a meaningful commit.

Commit messages must describe the actual implementation.

Good examples:

    fix: resolve QR auto-scanning in check-in flow

    fix: prevent duplicate QR email dispatch

    fix: correct table reservation state synchronization

    feat: update check-in QR verification workflow

    fix: resolve admin session authorization mismatch

    feat: improve responsive tables layout

Do NOT use:

    update
    changes
    fixed
    latest
    test

When the same logical feature is synchronized to multiple repositories, use
the same logical commit description where appropriate.

